CGTK 1.4.0
==========

CGTK, the Classic GUI Toolkit, is GTK+ 1.2.10 and GLib 1.2.10 brought
to modern systems. This is its first release. The API is GTK+ 1.2's:
programs written for GTK+ 1.2 build against it with few changes or none.
The libraries are versioned 1.4 (libgtk-1.4, gtk+-1.4.pc), and the 1.2
pkg-config names, gtk-config, glib-config, gtk.m4 and glib.m4 are still
installed.

Drawing and windows
* GDK draws into framebuffers, and a window system is a backend chosen
  at run time (GDK_BACKEND): X11 and Wayland, either or both built in.
  Child windows are GDK's own, not the window system's.
* Running programs follow theme changes through sockets in
  $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cgtk.
* Wayland: xdg-shell toplevels and popups, window groups, client-side
  decorations, drag and drop, copy and paste with PRIMARY, text input,
  and wheel and touchpad scrolling.
* Scaling for displays above 96 dpi, on both backends, from the desktop's
  setting.
* Anti-aliased drawing for theme engines, and gdk_draw_rgba_image_scaled()
  for images with an alpha channel, laid over what is there.
* PNG files are read, with libpng: gdk_png_load() and
  gdk_png_load_from_data() give the pixels that
  gdk_draw_rgba_image_scaled() draws, and gdk_pixmap_create_from_png()
  a pixmap and its mask, as gdk_pixmap_create_from_xpm() does of an
  XPM file. gdk_png_load_straight() and
  gdk_png_load_from_data_straight() give the colours as the file has
  them, not multiplied by the alpha.
* SVG files are drawn, by an internal renderer, which is based on NanoSVG
  and needs no library: gdk_svg_load() and gdk_svg_load_from_data() read
  a picture, gdk_svg_render() and gdk_svg_render_area() draw it at any
  size into the same pixels, and gdk_pixmap_create_from_svg() makes a
  pixmap and its mask of one. gdk_svg_render_straight() and
  gdk_svg_render_area_straight() give the colours not multiplied by the
  alpha, for a program that lays its pictures over one another itself. It
  knows paths, shapes, strokes, fills, gradients and style sheets of plain
  class selectors, but not (yet) text, <use>, clipping, masks or filters.
* A window's icon in colour on X11, as _NET_WM_ICON, in the sizes a
  window manager and a panel choose from.
  gtk_window_set_default_icon_name(), once in main(), gives every
  window the icon the program is installed with, found by the name its
  desktop file has for it under icons/hicolor: the PNG files, or the
  SVG file drawn where there are none. gtk_window_set_icon_name() is
  for one window, and gdk_window_set_themed_icon() and
  gdk_window_set_icon_images() are what they call. On Wayland the
  icon is given by the xdg-toplevel-icon protocol to a compositor that
  has it (wayland-protocols 1.37 to build it in); one that has not
  finds the icon by the desktop file, as before.

Text
* All text is drawn with FreeType and found with fontconfig. Fonts are
  named "Sans 10", "DejaVu Sans Bold 11" and so on; X font names are
  still read, and bitmap fonts drawn as they were. The font selector
  shows the system's fonts.
* Text is UTF-8, or the locale's own encoding, and passes in and out of
  wide characters unchanged. GtkEntry and GtkText keep characters.
* Input methods through GtkIMContext, as in GTK+ 2: XIM on X11, the text
  input protocol on Wayland, and dead keys and compose with neither.
  The GTK+ 1.2 gdk_im_* and gdk_ic_* calls remain, and do nothing.
* Copy, cut and paste menus in GtkEntry and GtkText; UTF8_STRING first
  when pasting.
* GtkText scrolls sideways, by its horizontal adjustment, when line wrap
  is off. GTK+ 1.2 cut such lines off at the edge of the window.
* Undo and redo in GtkEntry and GtkText, and what is built on them: of
  what the user typed, cut, pasted or deleted, typing a word at a time,
  by Ctrl+Z, by Ctrl+Shift+Z or Ctrl+Y, and from the right-click menu.
  gtk_editable_undo(), gtk_editable_redo(), gtk_editable_can_undo()
  and gtk_editable_can_redo() are for a program's own menus, and a
  program's own changes are undone with the user's when made between
  gtk_editable_begin_user_action() and gtk_editable_end_user_action(),
  GTK+ 2's names. Its other changes cannot be undone and start the
  history afresh, and nothing is kept for an entry whose text is
  hidden.

Dialogs
* From GTK+ 2, by its names: gtk_dialog_add_button(), the "response"
  signal and gtk_dialog_run() for GtkDialog; and GtkMessageDialog,
  which says one thing and has the buttons to answer it. No icon is
  drawn in a message.
* The file selector is laid out anew: one list, of directories and then
  files, with sizes and dates and titles that sort it; places at the
  side, that the user adds to by the right button on a folder or on
  the places, and that are kept in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cgtk/bookmarks;
  back, forward and up; and the name
  and the kinds of file at the foot, beside OK and Cancel. Hidden files,
  renaming and deleting are in the list's menu. The functions and the
  fields of GtkFileSelection are those of GTK+ 1.2, dir_list is still
  filled, though it is not shown, and OK and Cancel are in a box of
  their own still, for programs that put a button of theirs with
  them: with a third in it the box is a row under the fields, as it
  was. New:
  gtk_file_selection_add_filter(), gtk_file_selection_set_show_hidden(),
  and, as in GTK+ 2, gtk_file_selection_set_select_multiple() and
  gtk_file_selection_get_selections().

GLib
* From GLib 2, by its names and with its arguments: GError; UTF-8
  strings (g_utf8_*, g_unichar_*); g_convert() and its relations, by
  iconv(); g_file_get_contents() and g_file_set_contents(), g_file_test(),
  g_build_filename(), g_mkdir_with_parents(), g_find_program_in_path();
  file: URIs; and the XDG directories (g_get_user_config_dir() and the
  rest). The C library says what a letter is: there are no tables of
  Unicode.
* Also from GLib 2: programs started, with pipes or without, and
  waited for (g_spawn_*, g_child_watch_add()); command lines taken apart
  as a shell takes them (g_shell_parse_argv(), g_shell_quote());
  key files, which .desktop files are (g_key_file_*); and
  g_ascii_strtod(), g_ascii_dtostr() and g_strv_length().
* gsize and gssize are size_t and its signed twin, not 32 bits.

Themes
* Eight built-in theme engines (all with Dark variants):
    Altus (the default, after Mist)
    Clarus (ported from Clearlooks)
    Fabrica (after Industrial),
    FenestraMM (after Windows 2000),
    Gelidus (after ThinIce),
    Metallum (after Metal),
    Unicus (after Adwaita)
    Priscus (the original GTK+ 1.2 built-in theme engine)
* cgtk-theme chooses the theme and font, and edits themes: their colours,
  a few at once or all of them, and their engines' options, which
  running programs follow as they change. Editing an installed theme
  makes a copy of it among the user's themes. Its Dark check box, or
  --dark and --light, chooses between a theme's light and dark versions.
* The font chosen in a theme is used in every locale; the per-locale
  gtkrc files with X fontsets are gone.
* The user's rc file is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gtk-1.0/gtkrc, which is
  ~/.config/gtk-1.0/gtkrc by default, and the user's themes are in
  $XDG_DATA_HOME/themes, ~/.local/share/themes by default. Loadable
  theme engines of the user's own go in $XDG_DATA_HOME/gtk-1.4/engines,
  ~/.local/share/gtk-1.4/engines by default. gtk_rc_get_user_file(),
  gtk_rc_get_user_theme_dir() and gtk_rc_get_user_module_dir() give
  them. ~/.gtkrc, ~/.themes and ~/.gtk-1.4/engines are not read.

New
* GtkGLArea, in libgtkgl-1.4, draws OpenGL through EGL on X11 and
  Wayland, paced to the display's refresh.

Removed
* Motif drag and drop, X Input extension devices (the core pointer is
  the one device), gxid, and the X_LOCALE and native-locale code.
* Static gravity: gdk_window_set_static_gravities does nothing, as in
  GTK+ 3, and gdk_window_set_child_shapes and merge_child_shapes do
  nothing.
* Ports to systems without C99 and POSIX, threadless GLib
  (--disable-threads) and builds without FreeType.
* The GTK+ 1.2 tutorial, FAQ and Texinfo manuals, and the notes in
  docs/, which described GTK+ 1.2 and were out of date. The README,
  NEWS, ChangeLog and other notes of GTK+ 1.2.10 and GLib 1.2.10 are
  in history/, as they were released.

Fixes, besides many found in porting
* Drag and drop by pointer, which dropped every grabbed event.
* A heap overflow from XPM images wider than 16383 pixels.
* GtkLayout scrolling, which never moved its children on X11.
* gtk_editable_insert_text with a length of -1, which overran the
  stack.
* g_strdup_printf and friends with %zu, %td and %jd.
* GtkHandleBox keeps its child inside its edges, so that a toolbar's
  buttons no longer cover them.
* gtk_editable_set_position on a GtkText with a position of -1, the
  end, as for GtkEntry, or past the end, which crashed.

Building
* One build for GLib and GTK+. No configure script is shipped: run
  autoreconf -vif first (see INSTALL). Cross-compiling is supported.
* POSIX threads, iconv, FreeType and fontconfig are required.
* Translations are UTF-8, under the domain cgtk. All 38 catalogues are
  complete, and every one was checked string by string: Serbian is in
  one script throughout, Romanian uses comma-below letters, and wrong
  or untranslated strings were fixed. The strings new in CGTK were
  machine translated and have not been reviewed by native speakers.
* The libraries and cgtk-theme are under the LGPL 2.1 or later.
